  "notes": {
    "block_layout": "DELIBERATE DEVIATION FROM THE DISPATCH INSTRUCTION. The dispatch said to re-assert 'block-layout --set Standard --yes'. FB_ShredderSequencer was measured Optimized BEFORE the import, so nothing was silently reverted and there was nothing to re-assert; --set Standard would have INTRODUCED an unrequested change, and openness-cli's own help says it DESTROYS RETAINED DATA on the next download - this FB's IO member is RETAIN SETPOINT. Gated with --expect Optimized instead (exit 0), which proves the property the rule actually cares about: the import did not move the layout. Optimized before, Optimized after.",
    "inconsistency_cascade": "The import left 4 dependents INCONSISTENT (iDB_ShredderSequencer, OB100, FC_ControlMain, FC_AlarmsMain). All 4 were consistent before the import (pre-import list had 0 INCONSISTENT), so the cascade was caused by this import and was cleared here.",
    "unexplained_clearing": "REPORTED, NOT EXPLAINED. sanity-check run 1 exited 9 listing those 4, and printed 'a device compile does NOT clear these, and re-running sanity-check will not either.' compile-all immediately after examined NOTHING (exit 14, compiled 0, entries []). sanity-check run 2 then reported INCONSISTENT: 0. Something cleared them and compile-all says it was not compile-all. The mechanism is not established from the tool output and is NOT asserted here; what IS falsified by observation is the printed guidance line, since re-running sanity-check is exactly what preceded them being clear.",
    "gate_strength": "Because that clearing is unexplained, the gate is NOT rested on a cleared flag: compile-all --force re-compiled a real work set of 43 objects, 0 withErrors, 0 stillInconsistent, nothingExamined false.",
    "not_done": "No download, no rig. simatic-ml/ deliberately NOT re-exported (ExportDriftDetectorTests pins FB_ShredderSequencer among six already-drifted blocks), so ir <-> simatic-ml drift for this block is now larger by this change and a re-export is owed whenever that baseline is refreshed."
